  {
    "question_id": "Q10.4",
    "class": 11,
    "subject": "Political Science",
    "chapter_number": 9,
    "chapter_name": "Constitution as a Living Document",
    "question_type": "conceptual",
    "question_text": "If amending power is with the elected representatives, judiciary should NOT have the power to decide the validity of amendments. Do you agree? Give your reasons in 100 words.",
    "question_latex": null,
    "mcq_options": [],
    "correct_option": null,
    "question_image": {
      "present": false,
      "description": null,
      "cloudinary_url": null,
      "latex_extracted": null,
      "source_page_number": null,
      "source_image_index": null,
      "ownership": "unknown"
    },
    "parts": [],
    "answer_text": "I do not agree with the statement that the judiciary should not have the power to decide the validity of amendments. The judiciary is authorised to interpret the Constitution. Judiciary as an institution is involved in actively interpreting the provisions of the Constitution while pronouncing its judgments. It is more acquainted with the fundamentals of the Constitution than any other body. This power of judiciary checks the inappropriate and arbitrary use of the amendments by any political party that is in the power and also defends the fundamental rights of the people.",
    "answer_latex": null,
    "steps": [],
    "final_answer": "The judiciary's power to interpret the Constitution is essential to protect fundamental rights and prevent arbitrary amendments.",
    "answer_image": {
      "present": false,
      "description": null,
